  "chapter": 62,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 2 Chapter 62\n\n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 6182, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to authoriz-\n        ing  school  districts  to  order  from  certain farmers without\n        requiring a waiver\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  Under current law, schools may purchase fresh, locally produced  agri-\ncultural products from individual New York State farm growers or produc-\ners,   or   from   associations   consisting   of   ten  or  fewer  farm\nowner/operators. A purchase from a larger association of farm growers or\nproducers requires a waiver from the State  Education  Department.  This\nbill would allow schools to continue purchasing food supplies from local\nfarm  growers  and producers - as they have been - but in more efficient\nquantities through purchases from larger associations.\n\n  I fully support the intent of this  bill.  As  drafted,  however,  the\npurchasing  limit  of $25,000 does not meet the needs of our schools and\nfarmers. By comparison, federal procurement rules allow for purchases of\nup to  $150,000  when  purchasing  for  federally-directed  school  meal\nprograms.\n\n  Increasing  the  purchasing  threshold  amount  will  allow schools to\npurchase larger quantities of New York state agricultural products. This\nwill  provide  local  farmers  with  a  broader  marketplace  for  their\nproducts.  Schools  will  also  be able to purchase larger quantities of\nnutritious food to support their meal programs. Finally, increasing  the\nthreshold will support my long-term goal of increasing local farm sourc-\ning for public school programs.\n\n  I  am  therefore  signing  this  bill  with the understanding that the\nLegislature has  agreed  to  a  chapter  amendment  raising  the  school\npurchasing threshold for NY agricultural products.\n\n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2016
 },
